from pathlib import Path
p=Path('docs/creative/GLOBAL_INTERFACE.md')
s=p.read_text(encoding='utf-8')
s=s.replace('Phase 04B refinement · 26 October 2026 · Implemented for creative review.', 'Phase 04B.4 · 27 October 2026 · Header/static composition approved; pointer correction implemented for review.')
old='The ordinary circle is 34px. Position follows with 0.14s power3.out quickTo smoothing. A signed-distance field attracts its visual target toward a bounded point in the Manifesto interval, up to 70% influence; expansion/release use a separate 0.52s power2.inOut engagement driver. Visibility has a 0.12s driver. Each property has one tween owner; there is no permanent custom animation loop.'
new='The ordinary circle is 34px. Phase 04B.4 uses two logical modes, NORMAL and MAGNETIC_REVEAL, classified synchronously from raw pointer coordinates. One reveal progress drives diameter, photograph opacity and inverse negative-layer opacity. Only a logical state change retargets its tween: 0.34s expansion / 0.24s release, power2.out. Pointer events continue to retarget position only, using 0.12s power3.out tracking. A 28% center-relative contraction plus safe bounds makes magnetic resistance perceptible throughout the interval. A 16px exit hysteresis band prevents edge flicker. Tuning values are grouped at the top of pointer.ts; no extra motion library or permanent custom animation loop exists.'
assert old in s
s=s.replace(old,new)
old='The measured LETS US / SEE. gap supplies horizontal bounds. The reading passage, observation, upper statement and footer supply vertical clearance. The target diameter starts from clamp(190px, 14.5vw, 300px), then is reduced to fit the actual empty area. It can therefore be smaller on constrained screens. The photo fades before the aperture can reach a glyph; the small negative state returns during release. A stationary image plane is registered to those bounds and translated inversely inside a fixed 320px clipping surface. Scaling the aperture does not attach or distort the image. Geometry reads occur on layout/scroll changes, not pointer ticks.'
new='The measured LETS US / SEE. gap supplies horizontal bounds. The reading passage, observation, upper statement and footer supply vertical clearance; the visible viewport and fixed header also bound the safe area. The target diameter starts from clamp(190px, 14.5vw, 300px), then is reduced to fit. The rendered circle is constrained to that area while progress is nonzero: there is no independent photo-clearance opacity gate. Release contracts safely, then resumes normal tracking from the actual last painted coordinate. A stationary image plane is translated inversely using that actual rendered position inside the fixed 320px clipping surface. Geometry reads occur on layout/scroll changes, not pointer ticks. A missing image retains the normal cursor and never enters a large unexplained black state.'
assert old in s
s=s.replace(old,new)
s=s.replace('## Future transition integration', 'Diagnostics are available without changing the interaction through `window.__stillformPointer.snapshot()`, `.transitions()` and `.tuning`. Snapshots expose raw/visual/target coordinates, region/safe bounds, mode, progress, diameter, both opacities, influence, geometry revision and tween activity. The transition ring is bounded to 80 entries. No production console or telemetry logging is added. The API is removed when the controller is ineligible/disposed.\n\n## Future transition integration')
s=s.replace('This removes photographic engagement while retaining the global small cursor. Restore true only when the Manifesto is settled.', 'This changes the logical mode immediately and contracts the photo over the release duration while retaining the global cursor. Wait for snapshot progress 0 if a transition needs the photographic layer fully clear. Restore true only when the Manifesto is settled.')
s=s.replace('[Implementation evidence and current limits](../qa/phase-04b-refinement/README.md).', '[Current pointer correction and evidence](../qa/phase-04b-4/README.md). [Historical header/refinement evidence](../qa/phase-04b-refinement/README.md).')
p.write_text(s,encoding='utf-8')
